---
// Ported from the Claude Design canvas artboard Build.dc.html. Edit the canvas, then re-port.
import BaseV2 from '../layouts/BaseV2.astro';
---
<BaseV2 title="For Business · Paramore.Design" description="Custom AI-powered tools that replace the stack of half-used SaaS small businesses pay for.">
  <section class="pd-wrap" data-screen-label="Hero">
    <div class="pd-topline"><span class="pd-kicker--accent" style="color: var(--color-accent-ink)">Now booking small business AI projects</span><span style="color: var(--color-text-faint)">For Business</span></div>
    <h1 class="pd-title" style="margin-top: 40px">AI tools, built<br>for the way your<br><span class="pd-accent">business actually runs.</span></h1>
    <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end; gap: 32px 64px; margin-top: 40px; padding-bottom: 8px">
      <div class="pd-lede">
        <p>You’re paying ten different tools to do one job each. I’m one designer-developer who builds custom software, powered by AI, that replaces the stack and fits how <em>you</em> actually work.</p>
        <p>No bloat. No retainers for features you’ll never use. Just the tool you wish existed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-btns">
        <a href="#contact" class="pd-btn pd-btn--primary">Book a 20-min call
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg>
        </a>
        <a href="#services" class="pd-btn">See how it works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="The Problem">
    <div class="pd-text" style="border-top: var(--pd-rule); padding-top: 40px">
      <div style="grid-column: span 2">
        <div class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent" style="margin-bottom: 20px; width: 100%">The Problem</div>
        <h2 class="pd-h2" style="width: 100%">You didn’t start a business to manage software.</h2>
      </div>
      
    </div>
    <div class="pd-cells pd-cells--wide" style="margin-top: 40px">
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3">Death by subscriptions</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">Scheduling here. Invoicing there. CRM somewhere else. Each tool used for one feature, and the bills add up to thousands a year.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3">Spreadsheet sprawl</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">Critical info lives in twelve different sheets, three inboxes, and one person’s head. Nothing talks to anything.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3">Built for someone else</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">Big platforms are built for the average customer. You’re not the average. The workflow you actually need doesn’t exist yet.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Recent Builds">
    <div class="pd-head"><span class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent">Recent Builds</span><a href="/work" class="pd-arrow-link">All projects →</a></div>
    <h2 class="pd-h2" style="margin: 32px 0 40px">Real tools, real businesses.</h2>
    <a href="/projects/the-tree-service" class="pd-card pd-split" style="margin-bottom: 56px">
      <div class="pd-frame"><img src="/assets/images/projects/TreeServiceHero.webp" alt="The Tree Service field tool" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10"></div>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
        <span class="pd-kicker">Client Project // Field Ops &amp; AI</span>
        <h3 class="pd-card__title" style="font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 52px)">The Tree Service</h3>
        <p class="pd-card__desc">Field-ops tool that replaced four SaaS subscriptions with one: equipment, fuel, AI-parsed receipts, and crew safety checklists. Built solo in four weeks.</p>
        <span class="pd-arrow-link">Read the case study →</span>
      </div>
    </a>
    <a href="#contact" class="pd-card pd-split pd-split--flip" style="margin-bottom: 56px">
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10">[Portal screenshot: blur names and wedding photos]</div>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
        <span class="pd-kicker">Client Project // Publishing Operations</span>
        <h3 class="pd-card__title" style="font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 52px)">Utah Valley Bride</h3>
        <p class="pd-card__desc">A submissions portal for a wedding magazine: intake, photo curation, copyright approvals, editor emails, and publishing status, in one place instead of a spreadsheet and an inbox. Live at portal.utahvalleybride.com with 663 submissions.</p>
        <p class="pd-card__desc" style="color: var(--color-text-faint)">Next.js · Supabase · Resend · Vercel</p>
      </div>
    </a>
    <div style="margin-bottom: 56px">
    <figure class="pd-testimonial" style="margin: 0">
      <div><div class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent">From a client</div><div class="pd-kicker" style="margin-top: 8px">[Pending Carys’s OK to quote]</div></div>
      <div>
        <blockquote>“The submission thing right now is just making our lives so much better. I’m so, so grateful.”</blockquote>
        <figcaption><strong>Carys</strong>, Owner, Utah Valley Bride, on the submissions portal I designed and built for the magazine.</figcaption>
      </div>
    </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-cards">
      <a href="/projects/mutual" class="pd-card">
        <div class="pd-frame"><img src="/assets/projects/mutual/MutualHero-wide.jpg" alt="Mutual app screens" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 3"></div>
        <span class="pd-kicker">Founder // 10 Years // Solo Designer</span>
        <h3 class="pd-card__title">Mutual</h3>
        <p class="pd-card__desc">Co-founder and sole founding designer of the #1 LDS dating app. Ten years owning every surface: UI, brand, design system, research.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/projects/mutual-design-system.html" class="pd-card">
        <div class="pd-frame"><img src="/assets/images/projects/MutualDesignSystemHero.jpg" alt="Mutual Design System live token explorer" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 3"></div>
        <span class="pd-kicker">Design System // Engineers &amp; AI Agents</span>
        <h3 class="pd-card__title">Mutual Design System</h3>
        <p class="pd-card__desc">3 brands, 6 themes, semantic tokens, and live WCAG contrast, structured so engineers and AI agents can build from one source.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="https://checkinapp.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="pd-card">
        <div class="pd-frame"><img src="/assets/projects/checkin/CheckinHero.jpg" alt="Checkin app campfire check-in flow" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 3"></div>
        <span class="pd-kicker">Personal Project // iOS &amp; Android</span>
        <h3 class="pd-card__title">Checkin</h3>
        <p class="pd-card__desc">Social coordination app where friends signal availability through campfire check-ins. Design, development, and product strategy, start to ship.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="services" class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="What I Do" style="padding-bottom: 0px">
    <div class="pd-text" style="border-top: var(--pd-rule); padding-top: 40px">
      <div style="grid-column: span 2">
        <div class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent" style="margin-bottom: 20px">What I Do</div>
        <h2 class="pd-h2">One person. Custom built. <br>AI inside.</h2>
      </div>
      
    </div>
    <p class="pd-lede" style="max-width: 1035px">I sit down with you, learn your business in plain language, then build software shaped around it. AI does the heavy lifting under the hood (drafting messages, parsing receipts, tracking inventory, summarizing leads) so the tool feels less like work and more like a smart assistant that already knows the job.</p><div class="pd-cells" style="margin-top: 40px">
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3">Replace the stack</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">One tool, your logo, your workflow. Built to do what your six current subscriptions do, minus the parts you never used.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3">AI that earns its keep</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">Auto-categorize expenses. Draft client follow-ups. Turn a photo of a receipt into a logged transaction. Real time saved, every day.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3">Designed, not just built</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">13 years of product design means tools your team will actually use, not abandoned three weeks in because the UI fights them.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3">You own it</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">No per-seat fees forever. No vendor lock-in. Build, ship, and let it run. I’m here when you want to grow it.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Built For">
    <div class="pd-head"><span class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent">Built For</span></div>
    <h2 class="pd-h2" style="margin: 32px 0 40px">Small businesses with real workflows.</h2>
    <div class="pd-cells">
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3" style="font-size: 24px">Trades &amp; services</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">Tree work, plumbing, HVAC, electricians. Crews, equipment, fuel, receipts, jobs, one place.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3" style="font-size: 24px">Yard &amp; property</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">Lawn care, landscaping, pool service. Routes, clients, equipment, recurring billing.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3" style="font-size: 24px">Real estate agents</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">Lead intake, follow-up drafts, property notes, custom client-facing pages.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3" style="font-size: 24px">Events &amp; magazines</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">Submissions, status, payments, scheduling, designer handoff. The thing your spreadsheet wishes it was.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3" style="font-size: 24px">Restaurants &amp; shops</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">Shift approvals, task lists, daily ops, employee comms, without buying a Fortune 500 platform.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="pd-h3" style="font-size: 24px">Founders with an idea</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">You’ve had the napkin sketch in your head for two years. Let’s make it real.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="How It Works">
    <div class="pd-head"><span class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent">How It Works</span></div>
    <h2 class="pd-h2" style="margin: 32px 0 40px">Four steps, no surprises.</h2>
    <div class="pd-cells">
      <div><span class="pd-step__num">01</span><h3 class="pd-h3">Talk</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">20 minutes, free. You walk me through what’s eating your time. I tell you, plainly, whether I can help.</p></div>
      <div><span class="pd-step__num">02</span><h3 class="pd-h3">Map</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">I sketch the tool, the AI pieces, what it replaces, and what it costs. Fixed price, not hourly.</p></div>
      <div><span class="pd-step__num">03</span><h3 class="pd-h3">Build</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">I design and build it. You see progress weekly. We adjust as you actually use it.</p></div>
      <div><span class="pd-step__num">04</span><h3 class="pd-h3">Ship</h3><p class="pd-cell__text">It’s yours. I stick around for tweaks and improvements when you want them, never on a meter.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section pd-section--last" data-screen-label="Clients">
    <div class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent" style="margin-bottom: 16px">Past clients &amp; teams // 13 years across brands you know</div>
    <div class="home-brands">
      <span>Mutual</span><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span>Ark Dating</span><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span>Nu Skin</span><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span>Angel Studios</span><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span>Tech 9</span><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span>Stotion</span><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span>Utah Valley Bride</span><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span>Paramore Real Estate</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="pd-poster" data-screen-label="Contact">
    <div class="pd-poster__inner">
      <div class="pd-kicker" style="margin-bottom: 24px">Let’s talk</div>
      <h2 class="pd-poster__title">Tell me what’s eating your week.</h2>
      <p style="margin-top: 28px; max-width: 58ch; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.5">Free 20-minute call. Bring the spreadsheet, the tool you hate, the workflow that’s held together with tape. I’ll tell you straight whether AI can fix it, and what it’d cost to find out.</p>
      <div class="pd-btns" style="margin-top: 36px">
        <a href="mailto:hparamore@gmail.com" class="pd-btn pd-btn--invert">Book a call
          <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg>
        </a>
        <a href="/work" class="pd-btn pd-btn--ghost-invert">See more work</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseV2>
